menu "CherryUSB Driver"

config BSP_USING_USB_MSC
    bool "Enable USB MSC (SD card as U-disk)"
    default n
    depends on !BSP_USING_USBD
    select RT_USING_CHERRYUSB
    select RT_CHERRYUSB_DEVICE
    select RT_CHERRYUSB_DEVICE_MSC
    select BSP_USING_SDIO
    help
        Enable CherryUSB MSC device mode, using SD card as a USB mass storage
        device (U-disk). When enabled, the SD card will appear as a removable
        disk on the connected computer via USB OTG FS port.

        IMPORTANT: After enabling this option, you MUST configure the following
        in "RT-Thread online packages" -> "system packages" -> "CherryUSB":

          1. Select usb device speed: FS
          2. Select usb device ip: dwc2_st
          3. Select usb device template: none (IMPORTANT!)

        You MUST select "none" for the template because this BSP provides its
        own MSC template with proper VID/PID for Windows recognition.

        Note: This conflicts with the legacy USB device stack (BSP_USING_USBD).
        If you need USB MSC, disable BSP_USING_USBD first.

        Warning: When both USB MSC and local DFS mount are active on the same
        SD card, data corruption may occur. Consider disabling
        BSP_SDCARD_AUTO_MOUNT if you primarily use the SD card as a U-disk.

if BSP_USING_USB_MSC

config BSP_USB_MSC_BLOCK_DEV_NAME
    string "Block device name for USB MSC"
    default "sd0"
    help
        The RT-Thread block device name to expose via USB MSC.
        Default is "sd0" which corresponds to the SD card via SDIO.

config BSP_USB_MSC_READ_ONLY
    bool "Mount as read-only U-disk"
    default n
    help
        If enabled, the USB MSC device will be read-only on the host PC side.
        This prevents accidental data corruption from the host while the
        SD card may also be mounted locally.

endif

endmenu
